# Maintain documentation

Follow **maintain-documentation** skill (altitude: orientation maps, not detail dumps; STE-flavored writing for new/edited docs).
Skill ADR: maintain-documentation/adr/001-documentation-altitude.md
Home ADR: ~/.cursor/docs/adr/0010-ste-writing-for-agent-docs.md

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Docs root (agents) | `.agents/docs/` |
| Hub doc | `.agents/docs/README.md` |
| ADRs | `.agents/docs/adr/` |
| Terminology | `.agents/docs/terminology.md` |
| Plans | `.agents/plans/` |
| Deferred issues | `.agents/issues/` |
| Human docs | `docs/`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` - do not edit |

## Altitude

Agent docs = orientation map. Details live in code, tests, and short ADRs.

**Update** hub/area docs only when a major block/boundary is missing or wrong, or when a shipped decision needs an ADR + thin pointer.

**Do not** store in area docs: version pins, ephemeral IDs, CSS/DOM dumps, changelogs, pilot metrics, full cookbooks, secrets, or planned behavior.

**Exception:** `terminology.md` may hold proposed + current + deprecated names for plans and docs. See rule `terminology.mdc` and home ADR 0016.

## Writing style (STE-flavored)

Apply the skill STE section and reference STE checklist to new and edited agent docs: active voice, sentence length caps, no marketing filler, self-lint before done. One name per thing via terminology.md.

